frac{a}{4}, \\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{4}\\right)\\) and coordinates of \\(D\\) are \\((a, \\sqrt{3}a)\\).\n   - Distance \\(BD\\) is calculated as:\n     \\[\n     BD = \\sqrt{\\left(a - \\frac{a}{4}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\sqrt{3}a - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{4}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{3a}{4}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}a}{4}\\right)^2} = \\frac{3a}{2}\n     \\]\n   - **Answer**: \\(\\boxed{\\dfrac{3a}{2}}\\)\n\n2) **Surface area generated by rotating \\(BD\\) around \\(OX\\)**:\n   - The surface area is calculated using the formula for the lateral surface area of a frustum of a cone:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Surface Area} = \\pi \\left(r_1 + r_2\\right) s\n     \\]\n   - Here, \\(r_1 = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{4}\\), \\(r_2 = \\sqrt{3}a\\), and \\(s = \\frac{3a}{2}\\) (slant height).\n   - Calculation:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Surface Area} = \\pi \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{4} + \\sqrt{3}a\\right) \\cdot \\frac{3a}{2} = \\pi \\cdot \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}a}{4} \\cdot \\frac{3a}{2} = \\frac{15\\sqrt{3}}{8} \\pi a^2\n     \\]\n   - **Answer**: \\(\\boxed{\\dfrac{15\\sqrt{3}}{8} \\pi a^2}\\)\n\n3) **Volume generated by rotating triangle \\(ABD\\) around \\(OX\\)**:\n   - Using Pappus's theorem, the volume is the product of the area of the triangle and the distance traveled by its centroid.\n   - Area of triangle \\(ABD\\):\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| a \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{4} - \\sqrt{3}a\\right) + \\frac{a}{4} \\left(\\sqrt{3}a - 0\\right) + a \\left(0 - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}a}{4}\\right) \\right| = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}a^2}{8}\n     \\]\n   - Centroid coordinates: \\(\\left(\\frac{3a}{4}, \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}a}{12}\\right)\\)\n   - Distance traveled by centroid: \\(2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}a}{12} = \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}\\pi a}{6}\\)\n   - Volume:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Volume} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}a^2}{8} \\cdot \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}\\pi a}{6} = \\frac{15\\pi a^3}{16}\n     \\]\n   - **Answer**: \\(\\boxed{\\dfrac{15}{16} \\pi a^3}\\)", "ground_truth_solution": "\n####